## Structure

```
src/
├── main.ts                    ← starts the server (and ORM connection, if any)
├── app.ts                     ← builds the Fastify app; separate from main.ts so tests can import it directly
├── config/env.ts               ← the only file that reads process.env
├── errors/                     ← custom error classes
├── shared/                     ← database/cache/auth/health clients used by more than one module
└── modules/<module>/
    ├── <module>.plugin.ts       ← public API — the only exported file
    ├── <module>.entity.ts       ← the model{{#if ormTypeorm}} (also the TypeORM entity){{/if}}
    ├── <module>.repository.ts   ← data access
    ├── <module>.service.ts      ← business logic
    ├── <module>.controller.ts   ← Fastify req/res handlers
    ├── <module>.routes.ts       ← route definitions (internal to plugin)
    └── dto/                     ← request/response DTOs
```

Each module is a Fastify plugin. The `.plugin.ts` is the **only public export** — all other files are private to the module. Cross-module communication happens through the plugin interface, never by importing another module's internals directly.

Call direction: `plugin` wires everything → `controller` → `service` → `repository`. A layer only ever talks to the one directly below it.

